<title>USA: Western Resources seeks to block ADT warrant.</title>
<headline>Western Resources seeks to block ADT warrant.</headline>
<dateline>TOPEKA, Kan. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Resources Inc said on Wednesday it seeks an expedited hearing to invalidate a warrant that ADT Ltd granted to Republic Industries Inc in what Western alleges is an improper attempt to resist ADT's acquistion by Western.</p>
<p>Western alleged ADT is improperly trying to block the acquisition by filing to register 15 million shares to cover the warrant granted to Republic Industries last July. If the warrant were exercised, ADT Chairman Michael Ashcroft would have a proxy to vote the shares for two years, according to Western.</p>
<p>Western filed a request for an expedited hearing in a U.S. District Court in Florida to have the warrant invalidated.</p>
<p>ADT officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
